      "a": "wer:\nParagraph 1 (Page 180)\n:\nAfter independence, our country has fought several wars to safeguard its borders, territorial unity, and its people.\nThis made me think about the courageous Indians who stood up for the nation.\nParagraph 6 (Page 181):\nIt was reassuring to learn that the government has acknowledged and honoured the sacrifices of our brave soldiers.\nParagraph 9 (Page 182):\nThis deeply moved me and also inspired him.\nParagraph 12 (Page 183):\nThe scene felt truly grand and filled me with immense pride for our country.\nParagraph 19 (Page 185):\nThe overall atmosphere created a powerful emotional impact and was visually unforgettable.\nParagraph 20 (Page 185):\nIt was painful to reflect on the huge destruction and loss of lives caused by wars.\nParagraph 22 (Page 185) (Gratitude):\nI plan to give a presentation on Major Padmapani Achaiya, who fought for India in the 1999 Kargil War and received the Maha Vir Chakra.\nParagraph 25 (Page 187):\nI ended up writing a long letter because I couldn’t resist sharing this uplifting and memorable experience with you.\nIII. Which is India’s highest gallantry award?\nAnswer:\nIndia’s highest gallantry award is the Param Vir Chakra (PVC).\nIV. How would Ananda feel after reading this letter?\nAnswer:\nAnanda will be pleased to read the letter and will enjoy learning about Soumya’s experience of visiting the National War Memorial in Delhi.\nV. Do you think Soumya enjoyed writing this letter? Why or why not?\nAnswer:\nYes, Soumya seems to have enjoyed writing the letter because she was eager and excited to share her inspiring visit with her friend Ananda.\nClass 7 English A Homage to Our Brave Soldiers Question Answer – Let us discuss (Page 192)\nI. Why was Ananda reminded of the poem ‘Pushp ki Abhilasha’?\nAnswer:\nDuring her stay in Chandigarh, Ananda visited the Bougainvillea Garden in Sector 3. She noticed people placing flowers and offering prayers as a mark of respect at the War Memorial. This scene reminded her of the poem ‘Pushp ki Abhilasha’.\nII. How does Soumya’s letter help Ananda in pursuing her hobby?\nAnswer:\nAnanda loved collecting stamps, a hobby known as philately. The envelopes of Soumya’s letters carried attractive stamps that added value to Ananda’s collection. In this way, Soumya’s letters supported Ananda in enjoying and continuing her hobby.\nIII. Ananda is inspired to act after reading the letter from Soumya. What actions does she intend to take up? Fill in the table citing the sentences from the text."
