      "q": "6. website\nhttps: / /www.mygov.in\nA Homage to Our Brave Soldiers Class 7 Questions and Answers – Let Us Think and Reflect\nI. Read the extracts given below and answer the questions that follow.\nQuestion 1. You can see the obelisk surrounded by wreaths that have been placed as a mark of respect. The lighting design is planned in such a way that it transforms the monument’s landscape as sunlight changes from dawn to dusk. It truly is a majestic site that filed me with pride for our nation. I was also overwhelmed by the interminable flame as a metaphor for eternal stories of courage and valour.\n(i) Complete the analogy with a word from the extract.\nflame: valour:: wreath: ______________",
      "a": "wer:\nhomage\n(ii) How does the lighting design make the monument visually appealing?\nAnswer:\nThe lighting design changes the monument’s landscape as sunlight changes from dawn to dusk. It makes the monument visually appealing.\n(iii) State whether the following sentence is a fact or an opinion.\nIt truly is a majestic site…\nAnswer:\na fact\n(iv) What does the everlasting flame suggest?\nAnswer:\nThe eternal flame symbolises that the courage and sacrifice of our soldiers will always be remembered and honoured.\n(v) Choose the correct option to complete the sentence\nAnswer:\nadmiring\nQuestion 2. I was happy to hear that you got an opportunity to- visit the National War Memorial. I have heard a lot about it. Some people might see a war memorial as just a monument, statue, an edifice to celebrate a war or victory and commemorate those who sacrificed their lives or got injured in the war. In my view, it is also an expression of deep gratitude for the supreme sacrifice made by our brave soldiers defending the sovereignty and integrity of the country\n(i) Choose a line from the extract which shows that Ananda was aware about the National War Memorial\nAnswer:\nThe line is, “I have heard a lot about it.”\n(ii) What might be the most likely reason for people to consider a war memorial as a monument?\nAnswer:\nPeople regard the War Memorial as a monument because it stands as a heartfelt tribute to the ultimate sacrifices of our soldiers who protected the nation’s sovereignty and unity.\n(iii) Fill in the blank with a suitable word from the extract.\nWe conduct special competitions at school to our Independence day.\nAnswer:\ncelebrate\n(iv) Select a phrase from the extract showing that Ananda is expressing an opinion.\nAnswer:\nThe phrase is ‘in my view’.\n(v) Complete the sentence with a suitable reason.\nAnanda refers to the sacrifice of soldiers as ‘supreme’ sacrifice because. ______________\nAnswer:\nthe soldiers gave their lives defending the country.\nII. Answer the following questions.\nQuestion 1. What is the significance of the National War Memorial?\nAnswer:\nThe National War Memorial is significant because it honours the courageous soldiers who gave their lives to protect the nation and reminds us of their supreme sacrifice.\nQuestion 2. Lance Naik Albert Ekka is an example of selflessness, deter¬mination, and exceptional courage. Elaborate.\nAnswer:\nLance Naik Albert Ekka showed true selflessness by storming an enemy bunker without thinking of his own safety. With strong determination, he attacked the position, eliminated two soldiers, and silenced the light machine gun. Even after being wounded, he continued to fight bravely, displaying extraordinary courage and an unshaken spirit.\nQuestion 3. Explain how the National War Memorial and Museum app will be helpful in spreading awareness about war heroes.-\nAnswer:\nThe National War Memorial and Museum app shows how many people sacrificed their lives while protecting the nation. In this way, it helps spread awareness about our war heroes.\nQuestion 4. Why is it our duty to pay homage to our brave soldiers?\nAnswer:\nThese soldiers sacrificed their lives so we can live in peace. Therefore, it is our responsibility to honour and pay homage to them.\nQuestion 5. What is the main idea of this text? How does it justify the title, ‘A Homage to our Brave Soldiers’?\nAnswer:\nThe text focuses on honouring the courage of our soldiers and drawing inspiration from their heroic actions. Therefore, the title ‘A Homage to Our Brave Soldier’ is appropriate and well-justified.\nQuestion 6. Why were the students awestruck and humbled? Explain in your own words.\nAnswer:\nThe students were filled with admiration as they learned about the war heroes’ courage. They also felt deeply humbled knowing that these great men laid down their lives so others in the country could live safely and peacefully.\nA Homage to Our Brave Soldiers Question Answer Class 7 – Let us learn (Pages 194—196)\nStudy the following words taken from the text.\ndisregard – inconsequential – immortal – undaunted\nThese words are made by adding word beginnings like dis-, in-, im-\nand un- to the root words regard, consequence, mortal, and daunt respectively. Such word beginnings are called prefixes.\ndis- + regard\nim- + mortal\nin- + consequential\nun- + daunted\nI. Match the prefixes with their meanings and the root words to create a new word in the table given below. An example has been done for you.\nAnswer:"
