      "q": "3. Indian Navy\nSham No Varunah (Be Auspicious Unto Us Oh Varuna)",
      "a": "wer:\nStudents should do it by themselves.\nII. India has many other Forces that serve the nation. For example, Central Reserve Police Force (CRPF).\nFind out about such Forces and discuss with the teacher.\nAnswer:\nYes, India has many other forces besides the Army, Navy, and Air Force that protect the country and support national security in different ways. Some of the major ones are:\nCRPF (Central Reserve Police Force)\n– Supports internal security, helps maintain law and order, and assists during emergencies and disaster relief.\nBSF (Border Security Force\n) – Secures India’s international borders and works to prevent cross-border threats and illegal activities.\nCISF (Central Industrial Security Force)\n– Protects key government institutions, airports, metro networks, and major public sector units.\nITBP (Indo-Tibetan Border Police)\n– Safeguards the India-China border and operates in tough high-altitude regions.\nSSB (Sashastra Seema Bal)\n– Guards the borders with Nepal and Bhutan and helps curb trafficking and smuggling.\nNSG (National Security Guard)\n– An elite counter-terror force, popularly called the Black Cats, trained for hostage rescue and high-risk operations.\nAssam Rifles\n– One of the oldest paramilitary forces, mainly responsible for maintaining peace and security in the Northeast.\nCoast Guard\n– Protects India’s maritime zones and conducts rescue and safety operations at sea.\nTogether, these forces play a vital role in ensuring India’s safety and smooth functioning.\nIII. Create a collage capturing the lives and stories of people that inspire us. In groups of four, prepare a collage on a chart paper ‘on any such person and present it in the class.\nAnswer:\nStudents should do it by themsleves.\nIV. Many women have joined the Armed Forces and are serving the nation. Have a discussion in the class with examples.\nAnswer:\nWomen have increasingly become an important part of India’s armed forces, serving the nation with pride, discipline, and bravery. They take up diverse responsibilities as pilots, engineers, doctors, and officers, standing shoulder to shoulder with men and proving their capability in every field. Their growing presence in the Army, Navy, and Air Force highlights meaningful steps towards gender equality and encourages young girls to aim high. By protecting the country and challenging old stereotypes, these courageous women show that dedication to the nation and true courage are never defined by gender.\nKey Concepts in NCERT Solutions Class 7 English Chapter 13 A Homage to Our Brave Soldiers\nDelve into\nNCERT Solutions Class 7 English Chapter 13\nand discover the heartfelt stories of India’s brave soldiers. Understanding the\nimportance of A Homage to Our Brave Soldiers\nwill help build your appreciation and writing skills for exams and beyond.\nThis chapter encourages students to\nexpress gratitude\nand reflect on the sacrifices made by real-life heroes. Engaging with the chapter helps improve comprehension and enriches your exam responses for the 2026-27 academic year.\nPractice all\nexercise-based solutions\nand review the patriotic themes. Boost your preparation for English assessments by focusing on how these acts of bravery inspire us every day. Consistent revision leads to greater confidence and success."
